---
// /support — a single page of prose and one outbound link.
//
// Reuses the Legal layout for its prose typography and standalone-page chrome
// (Nav without section anchors, LegalFooter). Legal takes frontmatter because
// its other users are markdown pages; here we pass the same shape by hand.
//
// The Stripe link is outbound-only, so donate.stripe.com is listed under
// allowedHosts in policy.config.json rather than processors.
import Legal from "../layouts/Legal.astro";

const frontmatter = {
  title: "Support — Saboteur",
  description:
    "Saboteur is a solo endeavor, and I release whatever I can for free. If my work helps you, here is how to support it, or how to help at no cost.",
};
---
<Legal frontmatter={frontmatter}>
  <h1>Support Saboteur</h1>

  <p>
    Saboteur is a solo endeavor, and I release whatever I can for free. I won’t
    ever sell your data or engage in practices that make you a product.
  </p>

  <p>
    If you feel something I’ve made benefits you, or you generally want to
    support the work, you can help keep it going.
  </p>

  <p>
    <a href="https://donate.stripe.com/00w8wR9UNg1k5V5crXc7u00" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Support Saboteur →</a>
  </p>

  <p>
    <strong>Where it goes:</strong> Cloud Infrastructure, development costs, and
    time to research &amp; build instead of taking on other work, so I can focus
    on providing tools that make your creative work easier to create and manage.
  </p>

  <p>
    Support doesn’t unlock any special features and supporters aren’t treated
    differently. Your support is a way to show thanks and appreciation. It’s not
    a purchase.
  </p>

  <p>
    Not in a position to chip in? I’ve been there. Telling someone about the
    apps I’m working on, pointing people toward Saboteur, or reporting a bug
    helps just as much.
  </p>

  <p>
    Saboteur LLC is a business, not a nonprofit. Contributions aren’t
    tax-deductible.
  </p>
</Legal>
